  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 PM CST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nTemperatures and wind will be the main focus through Friday.\nNormal highs this time of year range from about 38 to 44 degrees.\nForecast highs for Wednesday are in the mid-50s, followed by a\nthree day stretch of highs in the mid 50s to low 60s from Thursday\nthrough Saturday. Overnight lows will also be mild. Saturday\nmorning holds the best chance to see a few record high minimum\ntemperatures, provided it does not cool off too fast before \nmidnight. This same pattern contributing to the mild conditions \nwill also allow for windy conditions at times, especially from \nlate morning through sunset each day, as southwest winds gust from\nabout 20 to 30 mph. This is low-impact to most, but something to \nconsider for any loose outdoor decorations. \n\nSeveral model cycles have kept the Thu-Fri weather system well \nnorth of the forecast area now. Confidence in dry weather through \nFriday has increased. \n\nWeekend precipitation potential remains about the same, although \ntiming has once again slowed down just a bit, with the most likely\ntiming of rain from 3PM Sat through Noon Sun. The probability for\nany measurable rain sits at 80-90% area-wide, while the \nprobability for at least 0.50\" of rain is 20-50%. \n\nCooler air wrapping around the departing low keeps a small snow\nchance in far north-central WI Sunday afternoon and evening.\nProbabilities for 0.1\" of snow in far north-central WI (mainly \nVilas County) is still 20-50%, and drop off pretty fast to the \nsouth. Potential for 1\" of snow in Vilas County is 10-20%.",
